course: dictionary
lesson: 1473
title: A word for disaster
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name very big, very serious events. Catastrophe is one of them: a sudden, terrible event that causes great damage or suffering, such as an earthquake or a flood. When you meet it, look at the clues around it to check its meaning.
explain: Read this: «Palestinians mourn the Nakba, «the catastrophe», when hundreds of thousands fled or were forced from their homes.» The words fled, forced and mourn tell you the event caused great suffering. Nakba is an Arabic word that means catastrophe, so the sentence uses both words for the same event.
explain: In everyday talk, people use catastrophe as a joke, for something that went very badly wrong. «The cake was a catastrophe» does not mean anyone was hurt. To check which meaning fits, swap in a meaning: does «the cake was a terrible disaster» still make sense? Then the joking meaning is the right one.
fact: Catastrophe is a noun, and catastrophic is the adjective, as in a catastrophic flood.
fact: «Catastrophe» means a sudden terrible event that causes great damage or suffering.
fact: Informally, «catastrophe» means something that has gone very badly wrong, as in «the cake was a catastrophe».
fact: Useful phrases: a natural catastrophe, end in catastrophe, and avert a catastrophe (to stop it from happening).
fact: «Nakba» is an Arabic word meaning catastrophe, used by Palestinians for the events of 1948.
exercise: «The town was hit by a catastrophe: the flood destroyed hundreds of homes.» What is a catastrophe here? | A quiet holiday by the sea | A happy street party | A new road opening | *A sudden terrible event that causes great damage
exercise: Mum says, «The burnt dinner was a catastrophe.» What does she mean? | The dinner was a great success | *Something went very badly wrong, said as a joke | A storm flooded the kitchen | A famous chef cooked the dinner
exercise: What is the adjective form of catastrophe? | catastrophe | catastrophes | *catastrophic | catastrophically
test:  Read: «Israel was founded in 1948; Palestinians mourn the Nakba, «the catastrophe», when hundreds of thousands fled or were forced from their homes.» Which clue shows the catastrophe caused great suffering? | Israel was founded in 1948 | Jewish people celebrate its independence | *Hundreds of thousands fled or were forced from their homes | The sentence has no clues
test:  In the phrase «avert a catastrophe», what does avert mean? | Make a film about | Cause | Watch carefully | *Stop or prevent
exam:  Which sentence uses catastrophe as a joke about something small? | «The flood ended in catastrophe.» | «The fire caused a catastrophe in the old town.» | *«Dad's pancakes were a catastrophe, but we ate them anyway.» | «The earthquake was a natural catastrophe.»
